<title>HONG KONG: HK Feb built units deals up 182 pct yr/yr in value.</title>
<headline>HK Feb built units deals up 182 pct yr/yr in value.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of transaction agreements for building units in Hong Kong in February fell 15.1 percent from January but rose 182.4 percent year on year to HK$73.5 billion, the government said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A total of 16,979 transaction agreements for building units, including residential and non-residential properties, were lodged with Hong Kong's Land Registry last month, it said.</p>
<p>That figure represented a fall of 13.9 per cent from the previous month and a rise of 85.1 per cent year-on-year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
